# 6a — Desperdicio. Sized `L` and split in two 2026-09-27, on the day it was taken.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE SEAM IS **EXCEPTION (1)** OF THE WORKING AGREEMENT AND NOT SIZE, AND THAT
# MATTERS BECAUSE THE AGREEMENT WAS AMENDED ON 2026-09-24: an `M` or an `L` is now one
# sitting, and a split must name a reason that is not size. **Half of this row is gated
# on a decision the owner owes and the other half is not.** `6a-i` ships a screen and no
# migration; `6a-ii` ships `0041` and a rule about who may see what, which are two of the
# four one-way doors the working prompt names.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ AND THE MIGRATION WAS NOT IN THE PLAN — IT WAS IN APPLIED SQL, WHICH IS THE HARDER
# DIRECTION BECAUSE NO CHECK READS A MIGRATION'S PROSE. Two comments put a view in this
# row by name: `0003:589` — *"the reason-and-quantity view for Desperdicio SHIPS WITH THAT
# SCREEN"* — and `0011:68` — *"a reason breakdown is a second view over waste_line alone,
# with no denominator — IT BELONGS WITH THE DESPERDICIO SCREEN (step 6)"*. `docs/PLAN.md`
# carried neither, and `6c`'s row claimed to be the first thing in step 6 that ships a
# migration. **The split is what a session found by reading the SQL instead of the row.**
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE MEASUREMENT THAT TURNED A SUSPICION INTO A SPLIT: an Empleada reading her own
# waste document gets **HTTP 200 and `"waste_line": []`** — a header with no products, not
# a refusal. `waste_select` admits every member and `waste_line_select` carries
# `has_role(…, 'manager')` (`0003:596`), because the LINE holds `unit_cost_net_per_base`.
# It is the only asymmetric pair in this schema, and `0040` kept it manager-and-above BY
# NAME while widening `purchase` on the owner's instruction.
#
# ⚠️ THE TWO HALVES ALSO HAVE DIFFERENT INSTRUMENTS, which is the `5d-iv` argument
# arriving a second time: `6a-i`'s capture screen is judged on a phone (`R9`, §2.11) and
# its wire is judged by `6a-i-waste-contract.sh`; `6a-ii`'s view is a VISIBILITY claim
# whose only instrument is a policy probe under `set role authenticated`. Putting them in
# one row means the fence nobody can see rides in on the back of the screen anybody can.
SPLIT_ID="6a"
SPLIT_GROUPS=( "6a|6a-i 6a-ii" )
DELIVERABLES=(
  # ⚠️ ONE SPELLING PER ROW, and never an alternation: a bare `|` in the regex field
  # truncates the entry and it fails downstream as a DROPPED deliverable, which reads
  # exactly like the defect this list exists to catch.
  "the capture screen itself — nine lines of Pendiente become a real screen|nine lines|6a-i"
  "reason-first — the cause asked BEFORE the catalog, which is all §2.8 specifies|reason-first|6a-i"
  "the five causes as data, and the payload key 0019 reads them under|waste.ts|6a-i"
  "one cause per document rather than one per line|ONE CAUSE PER DOCUMENT|6a-i"
  "a third cart scope, because a write-off is a third DOCUMENT and not a third arithmetic|third cart scope|6a-i"
  "no peso total anywhere on the screen — área 9's ruling of 2026-09-14|NO PESO TOTAL|6a-i"
  "an unpriced product's loss sent at zero rather than refused|UNPRICED_WASTE|6a-i"
  "the contract check over real HTTP — the only instrument the wire gets|6a-i-waste-contract|6a-i"
  # ⚠️ ROWS BELOW ARE `6a-ii`'s, AND THE FIRST OF THEM IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS FILE
  # EXISTS: a session that took `6a` as one row would have written the view without
  # anybody ruling on who may read it.
  "the reason-and-quantity view — 0041, and it carries no cost column|0041|6a-ii"
  "DocumentKind gaining a third member, which @/api/documents was written to accept|DocumentKind|6a-ii"
  "waste in Lo último, which closes the gap 5h-ii-a named|Lo último|6a-ii"
  "Eliminar over void_transaction, which already works for a cashier today|Eliminar|6a-ii"
  "Corregir, which needs the lines and therefore needs the view|Corregir|6a-ii"
)
PHRASES=(
  "6a-i|F|ships no migration|A POSITIVE assertion because merging is automated: a child that quietly grew a migration is repaired only by a fix-forward migration, never by an edit. It matters more here than in most rows, because the SIBLING ships one — so 'this row has no migration' has stopped being true of the parent, and only the child can say it."
  "6a-i|F|NO PESO TOTAL|Área 9's ruling of 2026-09-14 names this screen: Números and Desperdicio show waste as QUANTITY and not as cost or as a rate, until something fixes 0011. It is the half a session would leave in by copying vender.tsx, and C8.2's deliberately short catalog is what makes it wrong — a peso figure here reads \$0.00 for exactly the products most likely to spoil, which the ruling calls the one thing worse than a number that is missing."
  "6a-i|F|ONE CAUSE PER DOCUMENT|The loudest decision taken on the owner's behalf, and it is reported rather than hidden. The schema PERMITS a mixed-cause document — measured: the same variant twice under two causes is two rows and a 200 — and §2.8 nevertheless calls this screen reason-first, the column asked BEFORE the product. Reversing it is a reason on CartLine and a composite line key, with no migration, because the schema already allows both."
  "6a-ii|F|0041|The migration this row ships, named so the gate cannot be mistaken for a convenience. A security_invoker view over waste_line is EMPTY for the person it exists for — a view is fenced by every join — so the shape is product_margin_daily's, a definer view stating its own predicate, and choosing it is choosing what a cashier may see."
  "6a-ii|F|BLOCKED|The gate is a question in ⛔ DECISIONS OWED and not a task ordering. A migration and a rule about who may see what are two of the four one-way doors, and after an automated merge undoing either costs a fix-forward migration rather than an edit."
)
EACH_CHILD_SAYS=(
  # ⚠️ NOT `ships no migration` HERE — that is `6a-i`'s alone and is asserted above.
  # ⚠️⚠️ AND THAT ABSENCE IS THE POINT OF THIS SPLIT: `5d-iv.split` could assert it of
  # BOTH children because neither shipped one. Here one child does, so a spec that
  # demanded the sentence of both would force `6a-ii` to carry a claim that is false.
  #
  # ⚠️⚠️ THE FIRST SPELLING WAS `Desperdicio` AND IT WAS A SENTINEL THE FALSIFIER COULD
  # NOT REMOVE — caught by `S9` on the first CI run, which is that harness doing exactly
  # its job. Mode `I` matches case-insensitively, `6a-i`'s row says `desperdicio.tsx`
  # twice, and stripping the one capitalised `Desperdicio` left the check green. **A
  # required statement whose phrase also occurs inside a filename is a statement nothing
  # can prove is load-bearing.**
  #
  # ⚠️ `waste_line_select` IS THE RIGHT ONE FOR A SECOND REASON BESIDES BEING UNIQUE: it
  # is the fence that caused this split. `6a-i` must say why it reads nothing back, and
  # `6a-ii` must say what it is working around — **so a session holding either row alone
  # knows the other exists and why.**
  "I|waste_line_select|The manager gate on waste_line that waste_select does not carry (0003:596) is the whole reason this row is two rows. A child that does not name it reads as a screen that simply forgot a list, and the next session would write the view without anybody ruling on who may read it."
)
